   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/ExteriorAlgebra/Basic.lean:79 `abbrev exteriorPower : Submodule R (ExteriorAlgebra R M) := LinearMap.range (\u03b9 R : M \u2192\u2097[R] ExteriorAlgebra R M) ^ n`; mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/DirectSum/Internal.lean:295 `instance nat_power_gradedMonoid ... (p : Submodule S R)` already covers `fun n => p ^ n`, which is why lines 64-65 here are a re-declaration; the repo's own Clifford code uses the raw expression (TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/CliffordAlgebra/Filtration.lean:370 `LinearMap.range (\u03b9 Q) ^ (k + 1)`).",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/SymmetricAlgebra/Homogeneous.lean",
   "fix": "Make it `abbrev homogeneousSubmodule (n : \u2115) : Submodule R (SymmetricAlgebra R M) := LinearMap.range (SymmetricAlgebra.\u03b9 R M) ^ n` (exactly Mathlib's `exteriorPower` pattern), and delete `homogeneousSubmodule_def`, which then becomes a pure restatement. Alternatively drop the wrapper and state `pbwHomogeneousComponentMap` on `LinearMap.range (SymmetricAlgebra.\u03b9 R L) ^ n` directly, using `TauCeti.Algebra.prod_map_mem_range_pow` and `span_prod_map_eq_range_pow` in place of the two specializations at lines 51 and 56.",
   "issue": "`homogeneousSubmodule R M n` is an opaque `noncomputable def` for `LinearMap.range (SymmetricAlgebra.\u03b9 R M) ^ n`. Because it is not reducible, Mathlib's `Submodule` power API and instances no longer apply to it: the PR must restate `Submodule.nat_power_gradedMonoid` at line 64, `homogeneousSubmodule_def` (line 46) exists only to unfold it, and every future use of `Submodule.pow_succ`, `Submodule.mul_mem_mul`, `pow_le_pow_right` on it will need a shadow lemma. This duplicates an existing API surface under a new name.",
   "line": "42"
  }
